# an ending
@title Ash
@bg field
@mood grief

narrate It worked. That is the truth and it should be said first.
narrate And then the Order came down off the ridge.
narrate Not in fury. Not as a punishment. They came down because the mandate was gone and forty thousand people were standing in a fold of ground that had been a sealed zone for twelve years.
narrate It was not a massacre. That word is too clean. It was a dispersal that went wrong, in the rain, in the dark, with nobody in charge of anything.
narrate Nine hundred people died in a field eleven miles north of nowhere, after the Fever had already ended.
narrate Corin survived. He did not know why, and he spent eleven years failing to work it out.
corin grieving "Nine hundred people died here after it was over. It was nobody's plan."
corin grieving "That's the part I want you to know. It was nobody's plan and it happened anyway, and the only thing any of us can do about it is say the number."

@ending ash
